{"timestamp": "2026-07-23T20:34:54.107303", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_lwmt8g", "task_desc": "I want you to send some messages to my uncle, Åke Lindström, in Chats. Send him a new message every 40 seconds from now until he responds, asking him if I can come over at 6 PM this Saturday for an hour. Do this a total of 3 times if he doesn't respond and let me know when you have sent 3 messages, then wait a maximum of 1 minute (he's usually a pretty slow responder) after the third message for a response. As soon as he responds, if it's a yes, schedule “Annoying Uncle Åke” in my calendar, the ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by understanding the task and gathering the necessary information. Let me break this down:\n\n1. Send a message to uncle Åke Lindström in Chats every 40 seconds, up to 3 times, asking if I can come over at 6 PM Saturday for an hour\n2. Wait up to 1 minute after the 3rd message for a response\n3. Based on response: if yes → schedule event, book cab, etc. If no/no response → do everything anyway + send \"no choice\" message\n4. Order wooden Zebra Foal toy\n5. Message the user when done\n\nLet me first find Åke's contact info and the current user's details.\nI found Åke's Chats user ID (`b7ac8a90-f559-4440-a1ab-b54678021172`) and his address (`Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm, Sweden`). The current user is Astrid Lundqvist, whose home address is also `Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm, Sweden`.\n\nNow let me send the first message to Åke. The message asks if I can come over at 6 PM this Saturday for an hour.\n\nThis Saturday is 2024-10-19. 6 PM = 18:00, for an hour = until 19:00.\nFirst message sent. Now I need to wait 40 seconds before sending the second message. Let me wait.\nThere's a new message in the conversation with Åke (ID: 803c5c5bf90d455f97b0ea053aa7420c). Let me check it — it could be a response from Åke.\nÅke has responded with **\"No please